export const content = "<p><strong>*Note: These are only recommendations and are based only from my experience staying in these accommodations.</strong></p>\n<p>Fukuoka City &#8211; Kyusu Region&#8217;s largest and busiest city. Home of the original Tonkotsu Ramen. Home of the largest Reclining Buddha in the world.</p>\n<p>Things to do here : links</p>\n<p><strong><a href=\"http://www.hostelworld.com/hosteldetails.php/Fukuoka-Hana-Hostel/Fukuoka-City/71709\">Fukuoka Hana Hostel</a> </strong>&#8211; asked why I chose a Hostel? It has a lot of advantage over Hotels like value for money, cleanliness, local flavor, social interaction etc. But the main reason was Hotel is more expensive in Japan and it will cost us triple the price. We just need a place to stay for the night since we&#8217;re leaving early in the morning and the location is very convenient since we are going to Nakasu River to have dinner in Yatai (walking distance from the Hostel). I make sure to read the reviews, feedbacks, the hostel&#8217;s facilities and their rules &amp; guidelines first before making a reservation.</p>\n<p><strong>Price:</strong>  1x night for 2 persons (currency convertion was made during the time we made the reservation)<br />\nPHP  2,800<br />\nor USD  59.5<br />\nor YEN  6,094</p>\n<p><strong>Check-in</strong> 3pm  &amp; <strong>Check-out</strong> 11am<br />\n<strong>Location</strong>: 4-213, Kamikawabata-machi, Hakata-ku, Fukuoka City, Japan<br />\n<strong>Getting there</strong>: We just took a taxi we payed around 2,500 Yen from Fukuoka Airport. The taxi dropped us off in the nearest street since they can&#8217;t go inside the shopping street. from there it only took us 2min walk going to the Hostel. You can also ride a train and just walk 10 minutes from the station.</p>\n<p>Where you can have a look for more details: <a href=\"http://www.hostelworld.com/hosteldetails.php/Fukuoka-Hana-Hostel/Fukuoka-City/71709\">Hana Hostel</a></p>\n<p>Hana Hostel is located in the middle of a shopping street in CBD of Fukuoka so there is no problem getting dinner &amp; shopping because it&#8217;s already there at the front of your door!</p>\n<p><img class=\"wp-image-830 aligncenter\" src=\"https://felixstatic.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/2016/06/IMG_20160414_200405.jpg\" alt=\"hana hostel accommodation airbnb fukuoka osaka tokyo japan\" width=\"776\" height=\"1380\" /></p>\n<p><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-831\" src=\"https://felixstatic.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/2016/06/IMG_20160414_200423.jpg\" alt=\"hana hostel accommodation airbnb fukuoka osaka tokyo japan\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /></p>\n<figure id=\"attachment_836\" style=\"width: 695px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img class=\"wp-image-836 \" src=\"https://felixstatic.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/2016/06/IMG_20160415_075508.jpg\" alt=\"hana hostel accommodation airbnb fukuoka osaka tokyo japan\" width=\"695\" height=\"1236\" /><figcaption class=\"wp-caption-text\">Double deck bed. very comfortable futon and thick blankets</figcaption></figure>\n<p><img class=\"wp-image-837 aligncenter\" src=\"https://felixstatic.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/2016/06/IMG_20160415_075524.jpg\" alt=\"hana hostel accommodation airbnb fukuoka osaka tokyo japan\" width=\"682\" height=\"1212\" /></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Tokyo</strong> &#8211; The capital &amp; busiest city of Japan.</p>\n<p>LINKS OF TOKYO ITINERARY</p>\n<p>We booked using <a href=\"https://www.airbnb.com.au/\">AirBNB</a>. Why? AirBNB is very popular for accommodation in Japan. It&#8217;s way cheaper and convenient than staying at those expensive Hotels. Worrying about security? Just make sure to research a lot on the host, the location, the apartment and the feedbacks &amp; reviews from the previous tenants. There&#8217;s also a super host feature where the host is rated high and is popular.</p>\n<p>We booked accommodation with <a href=\"https://www.airbnb.com.au/rooms/6577637\">Keiko &#8211; AirBNB Link</a><br />\n<strong>Price</strong>: 2x nights for 2 persons (currency convertion was made during the time we made the reservation)<br />\nPHP  3,600 x 2 nights = 7,200 PHP<br />\nor USD 76.63 x 2 nights = 153.26 USD<br />\nor YEN  9,758 x 2 nights = 19, 516 YEN<br />\n<strong>Location</strong>: Nishihara, Shibuya, Tokyo Japan<br />\n<strong>Check-in</strong> 3 pm and <strong>Check-out</strong> 10 am<br />\n<strong>Facitilies</strong>: Hot Shower<br />\nPortable wifi &#8211; I suggest to look for an apartment where they provide portable wifi so you can use it wherever you go. It&#8217;s very convenient so you won&#8217;t have to worry how to go to places. This made our stay a lot better and all our trips went smooth.<br />\nWashing machine<br />\nFridge<br />\nA/C<br />\nStove &#8211; We didn&#8217;t use. I suggest just have a meal at restaurants to experience local food better.<br />\n<strong>Getting there: </strong>We took subway from Shinjuku station and was walking distance from the nearest station (about 10min walk)</p>\n<p>Apartment was tidy &amp; clean. Beds were comfortable and has thick blankets.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<figure id=\"attachment_1189\" style=\"width: 670px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img class=\"wp-image-1189\" src=\"https://felixstatic.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/2016/06/IMG_20160415_194128_HDR.jpg\" alt=\"accommodation airbnb fukuoka osaka tokyo japan\" width=\"670\" height=\"1191\" /><figcaption class=\"wp-caption-text\">traditional futon bed. very comfortable with thick blankets.</figcaption></figure>\n<p><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-1191\" src=\"https://felixstatic.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/2016/06/IMG_20160415_194237_HDR.jpg\" alt=\"accommodation airbnb fukuoka osaka tokyo japan\" width=\"1279\" height=\"720\" /></p>\n<figure id=\"attachment_1192\" style=\"width: 652px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img class=\"wp-image-1192\" src=\"https://felixstatic.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/2016/06/IMG_20160415_194800_HDR.jpg\" alt=\"accommodation airbnb fukuoka osaka tokyo japan\" width=\"652\" height=\"1159\" /><figcaption class=\"wp-caption-text\">heated toilet</figcaption></figure>\n<figure id=\"attachment_1190\" style=\"width: 649px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img class=\"wp-image-1190\" src=\"https://felixstatic.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/2016/06/IMG_20160415_194207_HDR.jpg\" alt=\"accommodation airbnb fukuoka osaka tokyo japan\" width=\"649\" height=\"1153\" /><figcaption class=\"wp-caption-text\">hot and cold shower</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Osaka<br />\n</strong></p>\n<blockquote><p>It is the capital city of <a title=\"Osaka Prefecture\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Osaka_Prefecture\">Osaka Prefecture</a> and the largest component of the <a title=\"Keihanshin\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Keihanshin\">Keihanshin</a> Metropolitan Area, the <a title=\"List of metropolitan areas in Japan by population\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_metropolitan_areas_in_Japan_by_population\">second largest metropolitan area</a> in Japan and among the <a title=\"List of urban areas by population\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_urban_areas_by_population\">largest</a> in the world with over 19 million inhabitants &#8211; wikipedia.com</p></blockquote>\n<p>Things to do in Osaka&#8230;</p>\n<p>We booked accommodation with <a href=\"https://www.airbnb.com.au/rooms/10005475\">Momo &#8211; AirBNB Link</a><br />\n<strong>Price</strong>: 4x nights for 2 persons (currency convertion was made during the time we made the reservation)<br />\nPHP  8, 967<br />\nUSD  190.80<br />\nYEN  19, 516<br />\n<strong>Location</strong>: Nipponbashinishi, Osaka shi, Osaka Japan<br />\n<strong>Check-in</strong> 3 pm and <strong>Check-out</strong> 10 am<br />\n<strong>Facitilies</strong>: Hot Shower<br />\nIndoor wifi &#8211; my bad for not reading this one. I thought wifi was also portable just what we had with our apartment in Tokyo. So I made sure I searched all the places on my itinerary on the day otherwise I need to look for a free wifi spot.<br />\nWashing machine<br />\nFridge<br />\nA/C<br />\nSmall balcony<br />\n<strong>Getting there: </strong>We took subway from Osaka Shi station and made one transfer (no direct line going to the apartment nearest station)<br />\nApartment is close to Denden town, Namba &amp; Osaka Shinsekai</p>\n<p>Apartment was tidy &amp; clean. Beds were comfortable and has thick blankets. We turned on A/C at night time because we need to close the window since it was near the train line and we can heart the train&#8217;s noise.</p>\n<p><img class=\"wp-image-876 aligncenter\" src=\"https://felixstatic.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/2016/06/IMG_20160417_165743_HDR.jpg\" alt=\"hostel accommodation airbnb fukuoka osaka tokyo japan\" width=\"646\" height=\"1148\" /></p>\n<p><img class=\"wp-image-877 aligncenter\" src=\"https://felixstatic.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/2016/06/IMG_20160417_165757_HDR.jpg\" alt=\"accommodation airbnb fukuoka osaka tokyo japan\" width=\"649\" height=\"1155\" /></p>\n<figure id=\"attachment_878\" style=\"width: 1279px\" class=\"wp-caption alignnone\"><img class=\"wp-image-878 size-full\" src=\"https://felixstatic.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/2016/06/IMG_20160417_165823_HDR.jpg\" alt=\"accommodation airbnb fukuoka osaka tokyo japan\" width=\"1279\" height=\"720\" /><figcaption class=\"wp-caption-text\">two comfortable bed. actually it&#8217;s good for four people</figcaption></figure>\n<p><img class=\" wp-image-880 aligncenter\" src=\"https://felixstatic.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/2016/06/IMG_20160417_165849_HDR.jpg\" alt=\"accommodation airbnb fukuoka osaka tokyo japan\" width=\"769\" height=\"1367\" /></p>\n<figure id=\"attachment_879\" style=\"width: 775px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img class=\"wp-image-879\" src=\"https://felixstatic.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/2016/06/IMG_20160417_165840_HDR.jpg\" alt=\"accommodation airbnb fukuoka osaka tokyo japan\" width=\"775\" height=\"1378\" /><figcaption class=\"wp-caption-text\">hot and cold shower</figcaption></figure>\n<p>There&#8217;s one problem during our stay, using hot shower only takes several minutes before it becomes cold then we need to wait for it to be hot again. It was a bit annoying. We told the host about the issue but was not resolved during our stay. But overall it was a good place to stay.</p>\n<p><!--\n<strong>Other related blogs in Japan</strong>\nItineraries:\n<a href=\"https://whoisfelix.com/itinerary-in-osaka-dotonbori-osaka-castle-shinsekai/\">Things to do in Osaka, Japan\n</a><a href=\"https://whoisfelix.com/itinerary-in-tokyo-sensoji-temple-meiji-shrine-tsukiji-market-ueno-park-shinjuku-shibuya/\">Things to do in Tokyo, Japan</a>\n<a href=\"https://whoisfelix.com/itinerary-in-kyoto-golden-temple-bamboo-forest-fushimi-inari-shrine/\">Things to do in Kyoto, Japan\n</a><a href=\"https://whoisfelix.com/things-to-do-in-fukuoka-japan-nanzoin-temple-yatai-ippudo/\">Things to do in Fukuoka, Japan</a>\n\nFood:\n<a href=\"https://whoisfelix.com/best-tonkotsu-ramen-fukuoka-japan-yatai-ippudo-ramen-street/\">Where to get ramen in Fukuoka, Japan</a>\n<a href=\"https://whoisfelix.com/osaka-dotonbori-non-stop-eating/\">Eat til you drop in Dotonbori, Osaka, Japan</a>\n\n&nbsp;--></p>\n"
